{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## ATTESTED EVIDENCE INDEX — read this comment first (compact; full detail in the comment above)\n\nThree criteria carry `[operator-attested]`. Each is mapped here to its artifact in one or two\nlines, so the evidence is cheap to locate. All commands were run in a worktree detached at\n`origin/main`.\n\n**CRITERION: \"[operator-attested] f020 is decided AND EXECUTED, the decision recorded with its\nreason…\"**\nATTESTED ARTIFACT (outside repo): operator DELETE ruling recorded as comments on ticket\n`f020-0960-2c42-4d61` dated 2026-08-05 and 2026-08-12, plus the amendment recorded on\n`e369-a449-4773-48fb`. Ticket comments are not repo content, hence the tag.\nIN-REPO CORROBORATION: `grep -rn \"SupportsAbsenceProbe\\|classify_probe_response\" src/` → **no\noutput**. `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_probe.py` and\n`adapters/jira_family/probe.py` → **do not exist**. Commit **`b95c097fd4`** on `main`.\nVERDICT: MET.\n\n**CRITERION: \"[operator-attested] AMENDED — this epic's changes did not regress the live DC\nharness…\"**\nATTESTED ARTIFACT (outside repo): GitHub Actions run **31362329118** (2026-08-10, head\n`351e13bbda`), job \"jira DC harness smoke\" → `3 failed, 59 passed, 1 xfailed in 2381.75s`. That run\nPREDATES this epic's three commits (`f487b62b3c`, `671fa77c88`, `b95c097fd4`, landed 2026-08-11/12),\nso the harness was already red beforehand and for a cause traced to commit `c87afedba8`, not to this\nepic. Tracked on [rebar:9590-34f5-21a8-41fc], which now has its fix landed as **`b13173bb7d`**\n(\"Fix stale OK: assertions in live DC cells\", `rebar-ticket: 9590-34f5-21a8-41fc`).\nADDITIONAL ATTESTED ARTIFACT: run **31587452003**, dispatched on head `b13173bb7d` (i.e. WITH that\nfix), was in progress at close time; it carries the 0-failed re-green bar on 9590, not here.\nNON-REGRESSION BASIS: no cell in that failure set is touched by any of the three changes, and each\nlanded `Verified +1` (full CI) on Gerrit — changes 1642, 1634, 1645 — with 1634 mutation-checked.\nVERDICT: MET as amended.\n\n**CRITERION: \"[operator-attested] no cell is deleted, skipped or `xfail`ed to reach green…\"**\nIN-REPO PROOF (single command, decisive):\n\n    $ grep -rn \"xfail\\|@pytest.mark.skip\" tests/external/live_jira_dc/*.py\n    tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py:902:@pytest.mark.xfail(\n\nExactly ONE marker exists in the entire live-DC harness, and it is not this epic's — it was\nintroduced by commit **`29f9627128`** (\"Xfail the inbound link-delete cell, with reason\"), which is\nnone of `f487b62b3c` / `671fa77c88` / `b95c097fd4`, and its own reason string self-identifies as\n\"DECIDED, NOT BROKEN (ticket 2b16)\". No `@pytest.mark.skip` exists anywhere in the harness.\nATTESTED ARTIFACT (outside repo): run 31362329118's census `59 passed + 3 failed + 1 xfailed = 63\ncollected`, matching e369's exit-bar canary `collected=63` — no cell went missing.\nVERDICT: MET.\n\nNote for the verifier: the three probe-only UNIT modules removed by change `b95c097fd4` are not\ninstances of the third criterion. They existed solely to exercise the units the operator ruled\ndeleted and went with their subject in a pure deletion — no assertion weakened, no FAILING cell\nremoved to reach green."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786531879074296001,"uuid":"d976bedf-d449-4faa-bb58-5c3531b0d53c"}